  },
  {
    "fact_id": "bab83896-722c-4b11-9142-f0185a57ee46",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "The self-attention mechanism in transformers allows the model to weigh the importance of different input elements relative to each other.",
    "category": "technical",
    "importance": 0.51,
    "source_turn": 5,
    "created_at": 1774981189.940921,
    "access_count": 2
  },
  {
    "fact_id": "db8c16be-25d8-466c-aea8-887e39ea3f22",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "The self-attention mechanism involves query, key, and value vectors.",
    "category": "technical",
    "importance": 0.5610999999999999,
    "source_turn": 5,
    "created_at": 1774981189.940921,
    "access_count": 2
  },
  {
    "fact_id": "4d5a6250-dab9-4890-bf3a-2720059e28a0",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "The self-attention mechanism calculates the attention weights by taking the dot product of the query and key vectors and applying a softmax function.",
    "category": "technical",
    "importance": 0.5934999999999999,
    "source_turn": 5,
    "created_at": 1774981189.940921,
    "access_count": 2
  },
  {
    "fact_id": "a7b84065-2b22-49fe-9ed9-f064b42cb7d7",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "The attention weights are used to compute a weighted sum of the value vectors, which produces the output of the self-attention mechanism.",
    "category": "technical",
    "importance": 0.4864,
    "source_turn": 5,
    "created_at": 1774981189.940921,
    "access_count": 2
  },
  {
    "fact_id": "e2cc5e64-e809-4b91-9b1e-6f57b9afe538",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "Understanding the self-attention mechanism is crucial for mastering transformer architectures.",
    "category": "goal",
    "importance": 0.5299999999999999,
    "source_turn": 5,
    "created_at": 1774981189.940921,
    "access_count": 2
  },
  {
    "fact_id": "5468e0a1-10b0-4ae2-8ca9-5cadc17ec51a",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "The original transformer paper by Vaswani et al. provides a deeper understanding of the basics of transformer architectures.",
    "category": "technical",
    "importance": 0.34440000000000004,
    "source_turn": 5,
    "created_at": 1774981189.940921,
    "access_count": 1
  },
  {
    "fact_id": "11c4916a-21a5-4725-b6a6-4c89ec0fc5c3",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "Self-attention allows the model to attend to different parts of the input sequence simultaneously and weigh their importance.",
    "category": "technical",
    "importance": 0.5166999999999999,
    "source_turn": 7,
    "created_at": 1774981196.3416884,
    "access_count": 3
  },
  {
    "fact_id": "3f389d58-09b5-4f3a-a662-18f5b301b66f",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "Self-attention involves query, key, and value vectors derived from the input sequence itself.",
    "category": "technical",
    "importance": 0.5577,
    "source_turn": 7,
    "created_at": 1774981196.3416884,
    "access_count": 2
  },
  {
    "fact_id": "17912828-df98-4fcc-a9ac-fe7a3e52b323",
    "session_id": "demo-session",
    "text": "Cross-attention is used in the decoder part of the transformer model during training to attend to the output of the encoder.",
